### 4.1 Purpose and Scope

The full Monte Carlo grid of §3.7 is a multi-week computation (180 configurations × 100 replications = 18,000 runs). Before committing to that expense, we report the results of a **reduced grid** — 60 configurations × 20 replications = 1,200 runs — at the reduced specification of §3.7. This is sufficient to demonstrate the T-degradation, σ-degradation, density effect, and network-source robustness check. The ν grid (three levels) is deferred to the full study.

The reduced grid is reported in three parts:

